01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
customs agents after a bombing at the American embassy.

19
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Lee suspects that the crime is linked to the Triad crime lord Ricky Tan (Lone).

20
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
This film was filmed in Hong Kong, Los Angeles & Las Vegas.

21
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Rush Hour 2 opened on August 3, 2001, to generally mixed reviews.

22
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
The film was a commercial success, grossing $347.4 million worldwide,
making it the highest-grossing film in the franchise.

23
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
It also became the year's fifth-highest-grossing film domestically in the United States,
as well as the second-highest-grossing PG-13-rated film in that market.

24
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
A sequel, Rush Hour 3, was released on August 10, 2007.

25
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, los angeles, california,
criminal investigation, interracial friendship, buddy cop.

26
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The tone is lighthearted.
